# The Grid API. Used by BOTH bundles now: the admin console, and the public
# site's four forms and its testimonial strip (src/lib/publicApi.ts) - the
# marketing pages moved off Supabase, so this is the only backend they have.
#
# No default in code - a missing value fails loudly rather than silently
# pointing a production console at staging. On the public side an unset value
# disables the forms with a visible message rather than failing silently.
# NOTE: `api.gridmarketplace.in` does NOT exist (NXDOMAIN, checked 17 Sep
# 2026). The deployed value is the API Gateway stage below, which is what
# both bundles actually talk to. Copying the custom domain out of this file
# into a real deploy would break every request with "Could not reach the API".
VITE_API_URL=https://2lnlzb6lu6.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com

# The console's secret path segment, read by middleware.ts at request time.
#
# NOT prefixed VITE_, deliberately: only VITE_* variables reach the browser
# bundle, so this one never does. Set it in Vercel's project settings, never
# in a committed file.
#
# Unset means the console is unreachable, not open - middleware.ts 404s every
# admin-shaped path rather than falling back to serving it.
ADMIN_PATH_SEGMENT=change-me-to-something-unguessable

# Where middleware.ts fetches share-link previews from, server-side.
#
# Optional: falls back to VITE_API_URL, which is the same API. It exists as
# its own name because this one is read by middleware at request time on the
# server, not baked into a browser bundle at build time - so on Vercel it must
# be set in project settings, not only in a build-time .env.
#
# Unset means share links still work: they render a generic Grid card and
# still open the app. Only the per-listing title and photo are lost.
SHARE_PREVIEW_API_URL=https://2lnlzb6lu6.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
